{"lines":[{"t":"1718867188","w":0.069958845774332645,"c":0.5,"y":0.046511627815394085,"x":0.7716049391467531,"h":0.008720930389296444},{"w":0.057613169352213556,"c":1,"x":0.11728395020043644,"t":"Test 1","y":0.053779069624731557,"h":0.013081395583944722},{"y":0.097383720806202834,"w":0.21193415323893228,"t":"READING PASSAGE 2","x":0.11728395208423753,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1},{"y":0.1292697288541842,"w":0.77366256713867188,"h":0.017667844522968101,"c":1,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","x":0.11728394270159488},{"y":0.14680232543706795,"x":0.11728394960828926,"h":0.014563987898180697,"c":1,"w":0.15843621571858724,"t":"Passage 2 below."},{"w":0.47942387898763023,"t":"Stadiums: past, present and future","y":0.18895348815714552,"h":0.023355109952785114,"x":0.26748970647590115,"c":1},{"y":0.22673733776836602,"w":0.72427983601888024,"c":1,"x":0.16049382674245691,"h":0.01454173212759069,"t":"Stadiums are among the oldest forms of urban architecture: vast stadiums where the public"},{"y":0.24263839811321419,"c":1,"t":"could watch sporting events were at the centre of western city life as far back as the ancient","x":0.1604938258020594,"w":0.73045267740885411,"h":0.014723203769140158},{"y":0.25819949927823393,"h":0.019366743988648127,"t":"Greek and Roman Empires, well before the construction of the great medieval cathedrals and","c":1,"x":0.16041844821013626,"w":0.73469813028971354},{"c":1,"t":"the grand 19th- and 20th-century railway stations which dominated urban skylines in later eras.","w":0.73456792195638021,"h":0.01598837238037687,"x":0.15843620366367872,"y":0.27616279054710602},{"w":0.73662551879882809,"y":0.30232558127554743,"h":0.013081395583944611,"c":1,"t":"Today, however, stadiums are regarded with growing scepticism. Construction costs can soar","x":0.16255143800488214},{"w":0.72839508056640634,"t":"above £1 billion, and stadiums finished for major events such as the Olympic Games or the","h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"x":0.15843620446898352,"y":0.31831395335563806},{"x":0.16049382799775505,"y":0.3342167255821884,"w":0.49382715861002602,"t":"FIFA World Cup have notably fallen into disuse and disrepair.","c":1,"h":0.016195524146054296},{"c":1,"t":"But this need not be the case. History shows that stadiums can drive urban development and","y":0.35895170804583443,"x":0.16255143899457145,"h":0.01472320376914027,"w":0.73045267740885422},{"x":0.15843621355801019,"w":0.72427983601888024,"h":0.016195524146054074,"c":1,"t":"adapt to the culture of every age. Even today, architects and planners are finding new ways","y":0.37632508816668508},{"x":0.1584362255412583,"t":"to adapt the mono-functional sports arenas which became emblematic of modernisation","h":0.014534883982160851,"c":1,"y":0.39244186033143458,"w":0.7016460673014322},{"x":0.15843621365121474,"y":0.40988372078536739,"c":1,"h":0.01453488398216074,"t":"during the 20th century.","w":0.19547325134277344},{"y":0.43459302310936143,"w":0.68724278767903646,"h":0.01598837238037687,"t":"The amphitheatre* of Arles in southwest France, with a capacity of 25,000 spectators,","x":0.16049383237933171,"c":1},{"t":"is perhaps the best example of just how versatile stadiums can be. Built by the Romans in","y":0.45053003551047544,"w":0.71604939778645837,"h":0.016039732066986834,"c":1,"x":0.1584362065999744},{"c":1,"x":0.1584362194153085,"y":0.46643109566365926,"w":0.64403289794921881,"h":0.016195524146054074,"t":"90 AD, it became a fortress with four towers after the fifth century, and was then"},{"c":1,"y":0.48401162777409035,"w":0.70781890869140629,"t":"transformed into a village containing more than 200 houses. With the growing interest in","x":0.16049383773763026,"h":0.01453488398216074},{"t":"conservation during the 19th century, it was converted back into an arena for the staging of","w":0.72839502970377601,"y":0.50000000021811419,"x":0.15843623288473738,"h":0.015988371257085521,"c":1},{"w":0.73456792195638021,"t":"bullfights, thereby returning the structure to its original use as a venue for public spectacles.","y":0.51737338054948212,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1,"x":0.15843620351161539},{"t":"Another example is the imposing arena of Verona in northern Italy, with space for 30,000","x":0.16049382863650086,"y":0.54210836299858911,"h":0.016031172025610885,"c":1,"w":0.71193415323893228},{"c":1,"y":0.55948174313297794,"t":"spectators, which was built 60 years before the Arles amphitheatre and 40 years before","w":0.69341562906901044,"h":0.016195524146054185,"x":0.15843621829906851},{"w":0.72633743286132812,"x":0.16049383490678451,"y":0.57558139520288287,"t":"Rome's famous Colosseum. It has endured the centuries and is currently considered one of","c":1,"h":0.015996932421752819},{"y":0.59302325568046577,"x":0.158436206349618,"w":0.54938273111979175,"c":1,"t":"the world's prime sites for opera, thanks to its outstanding acoustics.","h":0.01453488398216074},{"w":0.70188395182291674,"y":0.61473039958333286,"h":0.01904758997042133,"c":1,"t":"The area in the centre of the Italian town of Lucca, known as the Piazza dell'Anfiteatro,","x":0.16037509481802828},{"y":0.6322143699031475,"w":0.70576131184895818,"x":0.158436212053916,"h":0.017494931799503344,"t":"is yet another impressive example of an amphitheatre becoming absorbed into the fabric","c":1},{"h":0.016195524146054185,"x":0.15843620195877767,"y":0.64958775026589644,"w":0.68930043538411456,"t":"of the city. The site evolved in a similar way to Arles and was progressively filled with","c":1},{"x":0.15843620258095323,"t":"buildings from the Middle Ages until the 19th century, variously used as houses, a salt depot","w":0.74074076334635419,"c":1,"y":0.66715116264467655,"h":0.016005492463128768},{"t":"and a prison. But rather than reverting to an arena, it became a market square, designed","h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"w":0.69547322591145844,"y":0.68459302312297621,"x":0.16049383961974806},{"x":0.15843622550443398,"t":"by Romanticist architect Lorenzo Nottolini. Today, the ruins of the amphitheatre remain","w":0.7016460673014322,"h":0.014723203769140158,"y":0.70053003552944249,"c":1},{"y":0.71460226477903943,"t":"embedded in the various shops and residences surrounding the public square.","w":0.61753372192382816,"h":0.017479878572749241,"c":1,"x":0.16040245399025271},{"t":"There are many similarities between modern stadiums and the ancient amphitheatres","y":0.74116607774687493,"x":0.16049383429095437,"w":0.67489710489908861,"h":0.016195524146054185,"c":1},{"w":0.7408691914876302,"t":"intended for games. But some of the flexibility was lost at the beginning of the 20th century,","x":0.15837545223162691,"c":1,"y":0.75720914189366295,"h":0.017548755425586871},{"t":"as stadiums were developed using new products such as steel and reinforced concrete, and","x":0.16049383589253588,"y":0.77470930219198775,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"w":0.72016459147135414},{"y":0.79210836301049647,"t":"made use of bright lights for night-time matches.","c":1,"w":0.3971193440755208,"h":0.014723203769140158,"x":0.15843621263302149},{"c":1,"y":0.83421672563648708,"w":0.76748972574869778,"t":"* amphitheatre: (especially in Greek and Roman architecture) an open circular or oval building with a central space surrounded by tiers of","x":0.11728394360713243,"h":0.010306242638398189},{"w":0.39917696634928385,"h":0.010174418787512574,"y":0.84738372083538771,"x":0.12551439737331843,"t":"seats for spectators, for the presentation of dramatic or sporting events","c":1},{"h":0.013081395583944722,"x":0.11522633698313144,"w":0.026748971939086916,"t":"20","c":1,"y":0.86773255795657411},{"h":0.035152653221247165,"y":0.95314993691982619,"t":"IELTSXpress.com","c":1,"x":0.66984496081179823,"w":0.30619837443033859}],"h":3395,"w":2400}